<title>CANADA: Southam forms group to study Hollinger bid.</title>
<headline>Southam forms group to study Hollinger bid.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southam Inc said on Wednesday its board of directors has formed a special committee of independent directors to consider an offer to be made by an affiliate of Hollinger Inc to purchase the balance of the Southam shares not already controlled by Hollinger.</p>
<p>Southam said the special committee will be chaired by Donna Soble Kaufman, Yves Fortier and Stephen Jarislowsky.</p>
<p>The newspaper chain said it retained RBC Dominion Securities Inc as its financial adviser and Davies, Ward &amp; Beck as its legal adviser.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
